From: Liuqin Linux Kit contributors
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: liuqin: connect CPU thermal cooling

SM8450 describes CPU temperature trips but has no CPU cooling maps.
Connect every Liuqin CPU sensor's two existing passive trips to all CPUs
in its frequency policy, as the SM8150/SM8250 thermal descriptions do.
Listing every policy member also works if a different CPU registers the
shared cooling device. Poll every 250 ms while passive cooling is active
so step_wise can advance and release its frequency QoS constraint even
without a new threshold interrupt. Idle monitoring remains interrupt driven.

Keep the existing 90/95 C trips, 2 C hysteresis and 110 C critical trip.
The change is board-local and does not depend on ABL's root compatible.

